      "side": 1,
      "message": "A nonexistent CL now hangs for minutes instead of failing. `GetChangeDetail()` doesn\u0027t accept 404, and `ReadHttpResponse` retries 404s (replication lag) with backoff, so `--cl 999999999` didn\u0027t return within 150 s from either cwd (it logs \"A transient error occurred ... 404\" on each try). The old curl lookup failed right away. A typo in an agent\u0027s CL number shouldn\u0027t stall it this long.\n\nCould this lookup accept 404 and fail fast, e.g.:\n\n```python\nchange \u003d gerrit_util.ReadHttpJsonResponse(\n    gerrit_util.CreateHttpConn(effective_host, f\u0027changes/{cl_number}\u0027),\n    accept_statuses\u003d[200, 404])\nif not change:\n    raise ValueError(f\u0027CL {cl_number} not found on {effective_host}\u0027)\n```\n\nThe URL path (project already known) skips this lookup, and `GetMostRecentCqPatchset()` then hits the same retry inside `_GetChangeDetail`. Looking the change up once on both paths would cover that too.",
      "revId": "471fcc898d8f9f6c82e721324b2cd3c20903dd80",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
